      "icon": "🎬",
      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-10eros-beta5-turbo-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "TenStrip's 10Eros Max beta5 TURBO-hybrid (INT8, 21 GB): beta5 with the turbo delta fused into the checkpoint, run on the unmodified official graph at res_multistep / simple, 8 steps. No Turbo LoRA node, no second file.\n\nTwo-seed bake-off against the plain beta5 and the original 10Eros packs (RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB, 864x480, 5 s, vanilla ComfyUI, no attention accelerators): ~105 s per clip against ~200 s for 20-step beta5; on a face-visible image-to-video test it was sharper at frame 60 than the 20-step file (589 vs 502 Laplacian) with identity held and the scripted line word-perfect. One seed put the key light in frame on a locked-off portrait; a second did not, so treat composition as seed-dependent at 8 steps.\n\nThe author's own advice: full-step audio is better than turbo audio, and keep Spectrum and step caching OFF for reference-driven shots. Free system RAM matters more than VRAM; keep 16 GB+ free.\n\nVerified in SimpliGen 1.59.1 / engine v0.34.2 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti: 5 s at 864x480, 8 steps, 84 s warm with the app's Faster Attention on; the scripted line arrived word-perfect at the scripted time.",
